1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,072
AI shopping agents are starting to buy things

2
00:00:03,072 --> 00:00:06,144
on people's behalf, and when something goes wrong,

3
00:00:06,144 --> 00:00:08,064
they file real PayPal disputes.

4
00:00:08,064 --> 00:00:11,904
Warrant handles that, end to end, on live PayPal sandbox.

5
00:00:11,904 --> 00:00:13,395
Now the real flow.

6
00:00:13,395 --> 00:00:15,633
An agent checks out through Warrant,

7
00:00:15,633 --> 00:00:17,870
PayPal creates a real sandbox order,

8
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:21,598
and the buyer approves payment, just like a real purchase.

9
00:00:21,598 --> 00:00:22,344
Order captured.

10
00:00:22,784 --> 00:00:26,795
Here's the buyer filing a real dispute on PayPal sandbox.

11
00:00:26,795 --> 00:00:28,800
Under Unauthorized activity, they choose:

12
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,811
I suspect my account is being used by someone else,

13
00:00:32,811 --> 00:00:37,223
the same reason a real victim of account takeover would pick.

14
00:00:37,223 --> 00:00:39,629
They describe what happened and submit.

15
00:00:39,629 --> 00:00:43,640
PayPal confirms it immediately: a real case, filed, on record.

16
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:54,203
Warrant's webhook picks this up the moment PayPal fires it,

17
00:00:54,203 --> 00:00:56,495
no one imports anything by hand.

18
00:00:56,495 --> 00:00:59,168
It proposes a verdict in seconds: contest.

19
00:00:59,168 --> 00:01:02,275
Warrant shows exactly why -- the signed mandate,

20
00:01:02,275 --> 00:01:04,217
the evidence, the reasoning --

21
00:01:04,217 --> 00:01:07,712
and submits the contest straight back to PayPal's API.

22
00:01:07,712 --> 00:01:09,176
And here's the proof:

23
00:01:09,176 --> 00:01:12,104
PayPal's own case page updates to Under review

24
00:01:12,104 --> 00:01:14,300
with the evidence Warrant just submitted.

25
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:17,960
This isn't mocked -- it's a real dispute, really contested.

26
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,927
And it tracks all of this over time:

27
00:01:20,927 --> 00:01:23,153
which agents, which products, which outcomes.

28
00:01:23,153 --> 00:01:26,120
Every piece here is real. This is Warrant.

29
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:31,589
Every step here runs on real PayPal infrastructure:

30
00:01:31,589 --> 00:01:34,311
sandbox checkout and capture, verified webhooks,

31
00:01:34,311 --> 00:01:38,395
the real disputes API for contesting or accepting claims,

32
00:01:38,395 --> 00:01:42,024
and PayPal Login and Vault for autonomous charges.

33
00:01:42,024 --> 00:01:44,688
Four partner integrations make it work:

34
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:47,352
Channel3 verifies what was actually bought,

35
00:01:47,352 --> 00:01:49,572
Elastic surfaces similar past cases,

36
00:01:49,572 --> 00:01:51,792
Zapier automates the evidence loop,

37
00:01:51,792 --> 00:01:57,120
and AG Grid plus AG Studio give merchants a real analytics workbench.

38
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:02,010
That signature check isn't a flag in a database -- it's real.

39
00:02:02,010 --> 00:02:06,085
Every mandate is signed with the buyer's own Ed25519 key,

40
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:09,752
over canonical JSON, and checked against their registered key

41
00:02:09,752 --> 00:02:11,789
before anything is ever proposed.

42
00:02:11,789 --> 00:02:15,864
A tampered mandate or a wrong key is rejected outright.

43
00:02:15,864 --> 00:02:18,168
Gemini has no native MCP connector,

44
00:02:18,168 --> 00:02:20,472
so we built one from scratch,

45
00:02:20,472 --> 00:02:24,312
and it surfaced real bugs no unit test could catch:

46
00:02:24,312 --> 00:02:25,848
an async adapter mismatch,

47
00:02:25,848 --> 00:02:27,768
Gemini's own thought-signature replay requirement,

48
00:02:27,768 --> 00:02:31,608
and a schema bug that silently flattened a discriminated-union tool.

49
00:02:31,608 --> 00:02:35,448
All three only showed up in a live browser run.

50
00:02:35,448 --> 00:02:36,664
That's Warrant's edge:

51
00:02:36,664 --> 00:02:39,906
cryptographically signed spending limits an agent can't exceed,

52
00:02:39,906 --> 00:02:43,553
dispute defense that reacts in seconds instead of days,

53
00:02:43,553 --> 00:02:45,579
and full visibility for merchants,

54
00:02:45,579 --> 00:02:49,632
built for a future where AI agents do the shopping.
